  Ah, so NOW I see where you are coming from.  You believe that, contrary
to the CLL, "a word must never begin with a vowel", and that the denpa bu
must always be a glottal stop, not just a pause.  Both are contradicted by
Chapter 3 of the CLL, and lojban as it is actually used.  Since are talking
about some theoretical language that you use, and not lojban, there is no
point in continuing this discussion, as we are talking about two different
languages.
             --gejyspa


